# One package, explicit product boundaries

Odroe is a composable full-stack framework for Dart and Flutter products. One
package supplies the application model, typed routing, Query, RPC, server,
semantic documents, content, typed SQL, database drivers, and build tooling.
Each runtime remains visible through a focused public entrypoint.

## The default product path

```text
Flutter page
  → Query key and lifecycle
  → generated typed RPC reference
  → adapter-neutral ServerFunction
  → DatabaseModule
  → typed SQL
  → SQLite, PostgreSQL, MySQL/MariaDB, or D1
```

The generated full-stack starter proves that path with a typed `Post` list and
`CreatePost → Post` mutation on native SQLite and local Cloudflare D1. Generated
record codecs keep the domain types intact across Flutter, JSON, the server,
and typed SQL. It also renders a semantic Document at `/`, so the first route
has useful HTML before Flutter takes over.

The Flutter composition root is ordinary application code:

```dart
void main() {
  runApp(
    App(
      webPathUrls: true,
      modules: <Module>[
        QueryModule(),
        RpcModule.http(baseUri: rpcBaseUri()),
        DocumentModule(),
        RouterModule(routes: routeTree),
      ],
      builder: (app) => MaterialApp.router(
        routerConfig: app.read(routerKey),
      ),
    ),
  );
}
```

`rpcBaseUri()` keeps browser RPC on the current origin and requires an explicit
HTTP(S) origin on native clients. It never guesses that a mobile device can
reach its own loopback interface.

## One package does not mean one import

Use `odroe.dart` for neutral application composition, `router.dart` for route
contracts, and `query.dart` for asynchronous server state. Import Flutter, IO,
Fetch, FFI, and database drivers only at their owning boundary. This limits
reachable Dart code without pretending the package has optional dependencies:
pub still resolves one shared dependency graph.

The public [API entrypoint reference](/docs/reference/api) lists all 21 current
libraries and the behavior each owns.

## Current capability boundary

| Layer | Current product surface |
| --- | --- |
| Application | Typed modules, bindings, initialization, reverse-order disposal |
| Flutter | App composition, Router pages and shells, Query builders, Document handoff |
| Web | Semantic HTML, metadata, SSG/prerendering, MDC and Press content |
| Server | Typed routes/functions, middleware, cancellation, native and Fetch hosts |
| Data | Typed relational SQL; verified SQLite migrations and PostgreSQL; MySQL/MariaDB and D1 Preview |
| Build | Flutter pass-through, native server, static output, Cloudflare Worker |

Odroe does not currently claim a full identity-map ORM, automatic or
cross-provider schema migration, streaming database queries, mobile store
release automation, or provider-specific deployment beyond the native and
Cloudflare build targets. The native SQLite runner stays explicit and
application-SQL-first. Those limits are part of the product contract, not
footnotes.

